      "writtenOn": "2025-11-05T13:25:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Any reason why VM\u0027s guest_mmu_teardown_mc is initialized by pKVM-low, not by pKVM-high like vCPU\u0027s guest_mmu_memcache?",
      "revId": "5389d4173ae6cd3e2a12de74e43707bf37e145c9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "80d9e50f_2c1a7c3b",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 215,
      "author": {
        "id": 3484945
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-05T14:14:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `guest_mmu_memcache` is initialized with pages allocated by the host. The host initiates the memcache passing chain, which is then consumed by pKVM.\n\nIn contrast, the `guest_mmu_teardown_mc` is filled by pKVM. Here, pKVM initiates the memcache passing chain, which is then consumed by the host.\n\nGiven that pKVM is the initiator of the chain for `guest_mmu_teardown_mc`, I have decided to initialize this teardown memcache from `pKVM-low`, where the passing chain begins.\n\nDoes it make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "1abb4350_c0288527",
      "revId": "5389d4173ae6cd3e2a12de74e43707bf37e145c9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "28d49849_9e759b13",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 215,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-05T14:52:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My point is that guest_mmu_teardown_mc is a part of the host\u0027s kvm structure (pkvm_vm-\u003eshared_kvm), not pKVM\u0027s one. And philosophically, it is still the host that needs this memcache, just like it needs the guest_mmu_memcache. It is the host\u0027s job to allocate those pages, and it is the host\u0027s job to free them. :)\n\nAlso looks like pKVM-ARM initializes both memcaches in the host.\n\nAlthough functionally there should be no difference (as long as pKVM does this initialization after sharing + pinning the shared_kvm memory, per Chuanxiao\u0027s patches https://android-review.googlesource.com/q/topic:%22share-unshare%22), so if you insist, we can keep it as is.",
      "parentUuid": "80d9e50f_2c1a7c3b",
      "revId": "5389d4173ae6cd3e2a12de74e43707bf37e145c9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
